EmuSuNi (scripts/build-psp-core.sh applies this before its own patches): upstream PPSSPP's later
changes to its CPU depth rasterizer (compat.ini's SoftwareRasterDepth: Midnight Club: LA Remix,
Syphon Filter, Wipeout... - the lens flares), brought back to v1.20.4, as one git diff against it:
  7a13881245 DepthRaster: fix host buffer overflows in the depth raster queue
  5d0873d95d Depth raster: Clip to the drawing region as well as the scissor
  0edfd93a3a Depth raster: Stop a row once it has left the triangle
  cd59a16d85 GPU: Rasterize software depth on a worker thread (by hand: v1.20.4's texture cache and
             stats; the GPU's FlushPendingDrawing, which v1.20.4 hasn't, for the save states and the
             shutdown)
  a37e1f3660 GPU: Finish the depth raster when a list ends, before the CPU runs again
(hrydgard/ppsspp master, 2026-08-30 to 2026-10-16, GPL-2.0-or-later.) Upstream measured on Wipeout:
the rasterizer was ~40% of the emulation thread; on its own thread, 11% less time a frame on a phone.

